1
00:01:55,971 --> 00:01:59,971
NORTHERN ENGLAND EARLDOM OF NORTHUMBRIA
VIKINGS' BASE

2
00:02:02,641 --> 00:02:04,311
It was a Saturday.

3
00:02:04,851 --> 00:02:07,891
Vikings bathe on Saturdays.

4
00:02:11,361 --> 00:02:15,901
The English knew about this custom.

5
00:02:25,201 --> 00:02:28,001
Enemy attack.

6
00:02:35,461 --> 00:02:36,591
Burn them all.

7
00:02:36,671 --> 00:02:38,301
Don't spare the women or children.

8
00:02:38,921 --> 00:02:41,591
Kill them all. Those are the king's orders.

9
00:02:57,901 --> 00:02:59,531
SWORD

10
00:03:01,361 --> 00:03:04,071
Hang in there. This is it.

11
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:06,201
Yeah.

12
00:03:06,291 --> 00:03:08,411
I killed Snorre.

13
00:03:08,501 --> 00:03:09,711
Damn.

14
00:03:10,371 --> 00:03:12,331
All right. Spear troops, advance.

15
00:03:12,501 --> 00:03:14,251
Charge.

16
00:03:21,221 --> 00:03:24,511
The battlefield went that way.

17
00:03:25,431 --> 00:03:28,771
Why do I always get killed so fast?

18
00:03:29,221 --> 00:03:32,811
Dead men aren't supposed to talk, Thorfinn.

19
00:03:33,271 --> 00:03:37,071
You're always the first one to die, Faxi.

20
00:03:37,151 --> 00:03:38,441
Yeah.

21
00:03:39,111 --> 00:03:44,451
In Valhalla, in heaven,
you get to eat meat every day.

22
00:03:44,531 --> 00:03:48,661
You can't enter Valhalla
unless you're a strong warrior.

23
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:52,161
I see.

24
00:03:54,711 --> 00:03:58,631
I wonder if my mother and my sister
will get into Valhalla.

25
00:04:04,011 --> 00:04:05,471
Did they kill you, Thorfinn?

26
00:04:05,551 --> 00:04:08,181
If you die in the snow, you'll catch a cold.

27
00:04:12,141 --> 00:04:13,691
You're leaving tomorrow?

28
00:04:13,771 --> 00:04:16,691
You're so lucky. Where are you going this time?

29
00:04:17,191 --> 00:04:19,481
To Norway. I'm not going there for fun.

30
00:04:20,151 --> 00:04:21,441
I'm going to trade goods.

31
00:04:21,941 --> 00:04:26,201
I take wool and fur, and trade it for wine.

32
00:04:26,281 --> 00:04:27,951
Then I'm going too.

33
00:04:28,371 --> 00:04:32,121
No. What do you mean, "then"?
Don't say it so casually.

34
00:04:32,201 --> 00:04:33,911
What? You're so stingy.

35
00:04:34,001 --> 00:04:36,421
I don't care if you end up hitting an ice floe.

36
00:04:39,341 --> 00:04:42,091
I want to get some wine before the end of the year.

37
00:04:42,721 --> 00:04:44,801
I'm going to celebrate the birth of Jesus Christ

38
00:04:44,881 --> 00:04:47,181
with the people of my home country
with some wine.

39
00:04:47,681 --> 00:04:50,061
My father likes mead.

40
00:04:50,141 --> 00:04:51,311
Ask him for some.

41
00:04:52,851 --> 00:04:55,271
It has to be wine.

42
00:04:55,941 --> 00:04:59,731
I thought there'd be some wine in this village, though.

43
00:05:03,861 --> 00:05:04,741
Thorfinn.

44
00:05:05,361 --> 00:05:08,451
Can you pass on a message to your father for me?

45
00:05:08,531 --> 00:05:09,451
What?

46
00:05:10,121 --> 00:05:11,701
A warship has come.

47
00:05:23,671 --> 00:05:25,841
How's this, master?

48
00:05:25,921 --> 00:05:27,841
The leak's been fixed this time.

49
00:05:27,931 --> 00:05:29,761
Try putting some water in it.

50
00:05:33,431 --> 00:05:35,231
This is difficult.

51
00:05:35,311 --> 00:05:37,521
You put too much strength into it, Thors.

52
00:05:37,601 --> 00:05:38,901
Father.

53
00:05:39,311 --> 00:05:40,731
Father.

54
00:05:41,981 --> 00:05:43,401
I'm over here, Thorfinn.

55
00:05:43,861 --> 00:05:45,031
Father.

56
00:05:45,441 --> 00:05:48,411
Another warship came. It's huge.

57
00:06:06,131 --> 00:06:09,091
They asked for Thors the Troll.
They've been waiting there ever since.

58
00:06:09,721 --> 00:06:12,551
Thors? Are they talking about Thors?

59
00:06:12,641 --> 00:06:13,681
Troll?

60
00:06:13,971 --> 00:06:16,731
They're no amateurs.

61
00:06:17,271 --> 00:06:20,061
They're not like Halfdan's thugs.

62
00:06:21,651 --> 00:06:23,071
Oh, Thors.

63
00:06:23,731 --> 00:06:25,821
Are they planning to invade this village?

64
00:06:30,281 --> 00:06:31,661
Jomsvikings.

65
00:06:32,121 --> 00:06:33,581
I'm right here.

66
00:06:44,801 --> 00:06:46,341
They're bowing to Thors.

67
00:06:47,381 --> 00:06:50,471
I never imagined you'd come this far looking for me.

68
00:06:51,721 --> 00:06:52,801
Floki.

69
00:06:54,931 --> 00:06:58,561
We haven't seen each other
since the Norway campaign, Thors.

70
00:07:00,691 --> 00:07:03,941
I never imagined you'd be hiding here,
at the end of the earth.

71
00:07:04,981 --> 00:07:07,111
Tell me your business, Floki.

72
00:07:08,031 --> 00:07:10,991
Well, then. First give us your permission to land.

73
00:07:12,951 --> 00:07:15,371
Who is Thors?

74
00:07:16,201 --> 00:07:19,331
I heard he used to work on the battlefield
when he was young.

75
00:07:19,871 --> 00:07:21,421
They'll hear you, Ari.

76
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:25,381
He doesn't talk about himself much.

77
00:07:25,461 --> 00:07:27,671
Let me see.

78
00:07:28,051 --> 00:07:30,841
He said "Jomsvikings," right?

79
00:07:30,921 --> 00:07:32,051
Know anything about them?

80
00:07:32,131 --> 00:07:33,221
Not really...

81
00:07:34,261 --> 00:07:36,721
Father is angry.

82
00:07:37,971 --> 00:07:41,731
They made a surprise attack while they were bathing.

83
00:07:42,311 --> 00:07:47,651
Many Danes were killed
by English troops in Danelaw.

84
00:07:48,531 --> 00:07:50,111
Gunhilde,

85
00:07:50,491 --> 00:07:52,991
the sister of Sweyn,

86
00:07:53,071 --> 00:07:55,701
the King of Denmark, was one of the victims.

87
00:07:56,371 --> 00:07:58,201
Revenge for his sister.

88
00:07:59,241 --> 00:08:01,791
King Sweyn has a good excuse now.

89
00:08:02,411 --> 00:08:04,881
A big war is about to begin.

90
00:08:04,961 --> 00:08:07,091
It's time for us warriors to shine.

91
00:08:07,541 --> 00:08:08,801
-War?
-Quiet.

92
00:08:09,341 --> 00:08:12,471
The Jomsvikings will join the army of Denmark.

93
00:08:12,801 --> 00:08:16,721
Our invasion of England will begin
this coming spring.

94
00:08:17,801 --> 00:08:19,101
Do what you will.

95
00:08:19,561 --> 00:08:21,981
This is a small village
at the northern edge of the world.

96
00:08:22,231 --> 00:08:26,271
Whatever these big countries on the other side
of the North Sea decide, it's none of my business.

97
00:08:28,941 --> 00:08:30,941
That will not do.

98
00:08:31,441 --> 00:08:36,661
Our leader Sigvaldi ordered me
to gather the entire fleet at Jomsborg.

99
00:08:36,741 --> 00:08:38,121
No exceptions.

100
00:08:38,831 --> 00:08:40,081
Do you understand?

101
00:08:40,541 --> 00:08:44,411
Even if that man deserted the army.

102
00:08:47,081 --> 00:08:48,421
Deserted?

103
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:54,051
Captain of the Jomsvikings.

104
00:08:54,131 --> 00:08:55,631
Thors the Troll.

105
00:08:56,131 --> 00:08:58,011
This is a war...

106
00:08:59,641 --> 00:09:02,021
in which you too will fight.

107
00:09:14,651 --> 00:09:16,031
Thors.

108
00:09:16,451 --> 00:09:20,331
Our leader is doing this out of his own goodwill.

109
00:09:21,411 --> 00:09:24,371
After going missing 15 years ago,

110
00:09:24,451 --> 00:09:27,171
you have a chance
to return to the battlefield with honor.

111
00:09:27,581 --> 00:09:31,921
Our leader is willing to overlook everything.

112
00:09:32,001 --> 00:09:36,971
That's how much our leader wants you.

113
00:09:38,261 --> 00:09:42,181
You didn't have to come on a warship
just to tell me that.

114
00:09:42,261 --> 00:09:44,101
The villagers are afraid.

115
00:09:46,481 --> 00:09:50,061
You've changed a lot, Thors.

116
00:09:50,731 --> 00:09:53,361
Or did this village change you?

117
00:09:54,651 --> 00:09:56,191
-Run away.
-Run away.

118
00:09:56,821 --> 00:09:58,111
He's scary.

119
00:10:00,031 --> 00:10:01,031
This is a nice village.

120
00:10:01,531 --> 00:10:03,081
I can tell from the children.

121
00:10:03,661 --> 00:10:07,291
They've lived a life free from war, until today.

122
00:10:14,091 --> 00:10:15,711
Hear that? There's going to be a war.

123
00:10:15,801 --> 00:10:17,671
-Wow.
-This is my first war.

124
00:10:18,341 --> 00:10:22,301
He came all the way across the ocean to invite Thors.

125
00:10:22,391 --> 00:10:25,061
Your father is amazing.

126
00:10:27,181 --> 00:10:30,441
But I wonder if he'd take us with him.

127
00:10:30,521 --> 00:10:32,441
You have no chance. You're weak.

128
00:10:32,521 --> 00:10:36,111
-What are you talking about?
-You're no good unless you're strong.

129
00:10:36,191 --> 00:10:38,901
Well, I got that covered.

130
00:10:39,201 --> 00:10:41,821
You've never killed anyone, right?

131
00:10:41,911 --> 00:10:45,161
It all depends on whether
you've had that experience or not.

132
00:10:45,241 --> 00:10:46,201
Sorry.

133
00:10:54,251 --> 00:10:55,381
I'm not just...

134
00:10:56,131 --> 00:10:58,091
a powerless messenger, you know.

135
00:10:58,761 --> 00:11:02,261
If you're saying you're not going to fight in the war,

136
00:11:02,591 --> 00:11:06,681
I can't carry out my master's orders,
and our leader's reputation would be damaged.

137
00:11:07,471 --> 00:11:11,141
I can't go back empty-handed in a situation like that.

138
00:11:15,321 --> 00:11:16,941
You understand, don't you?

139
00:11:25,081 --> 00:11:26,911
The Jomsvikings.

140
00:11:27,701 --> 00:11:30,871
They're an army with a base in Jomsborg,

141
00:11:30,961 --> 00:11:32,791
a port town in Wendland.

142
00:11:33,381 --> 00:11:34,961
I never imagined

143
00:11:35,041 --> 00:11:36,841
that Thors used to be a Jomsviking.

144
00:11:37,251 --> 00:11:38,591
Are they strong?

145
00:11:38,671 --> 00:11:39,801
They're strong.

146
00:11:39,881 --> 00:11:41,431
They're so strong

147
00:11:41,511 --> 00:11:45,511
that the King of Wendland was unable
to collect taxes from them.

148
00:11:46,261 --> 00:11:49,311
They take pride in being the strongest army
in the Northern Sea.

149
00:11:49,391 --> 00:11:52,061
Withdraw. All troops, return to the ship.

150
00:11:54,271 --> 00:11:55,811
Withdraw.

151
00:12:02,901 --> 00:12:05,781
What was that just now? That was weird.

152
00:12:05,871 --> 00:12:07,871
You've been saved, Ari.

153
00:12:12,251 --> 00:12:14,041
Listen, villagers.

154
00:12:14,501 --> 00:12:16,921
I'm Floki of the Jomsvikings.

155
00:12:17,791 --> 00:12:19,841
At the orders of my master,

156
00:12:19,921 --> 00:12:21,341
I have come to this land

157
00:12:21,421 --> 00:12:24,091
to ask the hero Thors Snorresson to join our forces.

158
00:12:24,761 --> 00:12:25,841
Hero?

159
00:12:26,261 --> 00:12:27,681
Our leader has requested

160
00:12:27,761 --> 00:12:33,021
that Thors be provided with one warship.

161
00:12:33,601 --> 00:12:35,151
If you have what it takes,

162
00:12:35,231 --> 00:12:38,691
join Thors and come with us to Jomsborg.

163
00:12:46,741 --> 00:12:48,331
Farewell, Thors.

164
00:12:48,411 --> 00:12:50,911
We shall meet on the battlefield.

165
00:12:57,251 --> 00:12:59,341
We're going to war.

166
00:13:03,131 --> 00:13:06,431
-How many decades has it been?
-What?

167
00:13:06,511 --> 00:13:08,181
I'm going to kill them all.

168
00:13:08,261 --> 00:13:10,971
It'll be an honor to die on the battlefield.

169
00:13:11,061 --> 00:13:14,141
Let's get started right away.
Let's prepare the ships tomorrow.

170
00:13:19,151 --> 00:13:21,941
I guess you couldn't say no, Thors.

171
00:13:23,111 --> 00:13:25,201
I dragged the village into this.

172
00:13:29,121 --> 00:13:30,331
A long time ago,

173
00:13:30,411 --> 00:13:33,291
I used to earn my living by killing people.

174
00:13:34,331 --> 00:13:35,541
But one day...

175
00:13:36,711 --> 00:13:39,381
One day, I suddenly hated it all.

176
00:13:40,381 --> 00:13:41,501
I didn't want to kill

177
00:13:42,051 --> 00:13:43,421
or be killed.

178
00:13:44,631 --> 00:13:46,131
That's why I ran away

179
00:13:46,881 --> 00:13:48,301
from the battlefield.

180
00:13:53,181 --> 00:13:57,021
I thought I succeeded in making it look like I died.

181
00:13:57,521 --> 00:13:59,191
You could do that again.

182
00:14:02,481 --> 00:14:05,861
If I run away, this village will be punished in my place.

183
00:14:06,741 --> 00:14:10,031
The Jomsvikings never forgive deserters.

184
00:14:17,041 --> 00:14:18,671
The time has come

185
00:14:19,251 --> 00:14:22,171
for me to take responsibility
for what I've done.

186
00:14:29,801 --> 00:14:31,721
All right. Ready?

187
00:14:31,801 --> 00:14:33,811
One, two...

188
00:14:33,891 --> 00:14:35,931
Heave, ho.

189
00:14:36,471 --> 00:14:37,681
Heave, ho.

190
00:14:37,771 --> 00:14:39,311
Pull.

191
00:14:39,391 --> 00:14:41,271
Heave, ho.

192
00:14:41,351 --> 00:14:44,321
What? I thought you were leaving today, Leif.

193
00:14:44,771 --> 00:14:46,691
Thors asked me.

194
00:14:46,781 --> 00:14:49,491
I decided to join the fleet with that warship.

195
00:14:49,571 --> 00:14:50,701
I see.

196
00:14:50,781 --> 00:14:52,821
That would be safer.

197
00:14:53,201 --> 00:14:56,331
We'll protect you in a pinch.

198
00:14:57,581 --> 00:14:58,911
Here we go.

199
00:14:59,661 --> 00:15:00,961
I'm counting on you.

200
00:15:01,041 --> 00:15:02,751
Pull. Pull.

201
00:15:02,831 --> 00:15:04,091
Heave, ho.

202
00:15:04,171 --> 00:15:05,881
Though,

203
00:15:05,961 --> 00:15:08,301
everyone really does love war.

204
00:15:13,431 --> 00:15:15,311
You're so mean.

205
00:15:17,561 --> 00:15:19,601
Darn you, Thorfinn.

206
00:15:19,681 --> 00:15:21,101
Surround him.

207
00:15:22,151 --> 00:15:23,561
Bastard.

208
00:15:24,231 --> 00:15:26,781
We did it. I killed Thorfinn.

209
00:15:27,531 --> 00:15:28,901
That hurt.

210
00:15:28,991 --> 00:15:31,951
What's wrong with you? Die, Thorfinn.
You got killed just now.

211
00:15:32,361 --> 00:15:33,621
Follow the rules.

212
00:15:33,701 --> 00:15:35,701
That's right.

213
00:15:37,411 --> 00:15:38,371
What's wrong with you?

214
00:15:38,451 --> 00:15:39,581
Are you okay?

215
00:15:40,081 --> 00:15:41,461
Wait, Thorfinn.

216
00:15:48,421 --> 00:15:50,091
All right. Lift.

217
00:15:50,511 --> 00:15:53,591
One, two, three.

218
00:15:54,931 --> 00:15:56,851
All right. One more time.

219
00:15:57,101 --> 00:15:58,521
Thors.

220
00:15:58,811 --> 00:16:00,851
Can you take a look at this?

221
00:16:03,941 --> 00:16:05,111
The pain.

222
00:16:05,561 --> 00:16:06,861
It's broken.

223
00:16:06,941 --> 00:16:09,031
Someone hit too hard.
It's supposed to be a game.

224
00:16:10,401 --> 00:16:12,451
Keep the splint on for one month.

225
00:16:12,861 --> 00:16:14,861
Sorry, Thors.

226
00:16:14,951 --> 00:16:16,451
Thorfinn did it.

227
00:16:16,951 --> 00:16:18,621
He pisses me off.

228
00:16:18,701 --> 00:16:19,951
He's too rough.

229
00:16:20,041 --> 00:16:21,911
I'm never playing with him again.

230
00:16:22,581 --> 00:16:24,671
Is that true? My son did this?

231
00:16:25,041 --> 00:16:26,381
Yes.

232
00:16:26,501 --> 00:16:28,801
I'm sorry.

233
00:16:28,881 --> 00:16:30,421
I'll talk to him about this.

234
00:16:31,671 --> 00:16:32,881
Don't take it so seriously.

235
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:34,301
It's between the kids.

236
00:16:34,881 --> 00:16:36,971
He's only 6, right?

237
00:16:37,051 --> 00:16:39,891
If he can hurt kids
that are four or five years older than him,

238
00:16:39,971 --> 00:16:41,181
he must be pretty strong.

239
00:16:41,851 --> 00:16:44,021
He'll grow up to be a good fighter.

240
00:16:44,101 --> 00:16:47,151
He takes after you, Thors.

241
00:16:59,281 --> 00:17:01,371
You're giving me all of this, Dad?

242
00:17:02,331 --> 00:17:04,541
They're family treasures from my grandfather.

243
00:17:04,621 --> 00:17:06,461
Fight with all your might.

244
00:17:06,541 --> 00:17:07,541
Ari.

245
00:17:08,631 --> 00:17:10,131
You look good, Ari.

246
00:17:10,211 --> 00:17:11,801
Look at mine.

247
00:17:12,261 --> 00:17:15,301
It can cut off a horse's head in one stroke.

248
00:17:15,381 --> 00:17:16,841
Wow, it's huge.

249
00:17:16,931 --> 00:17:18,641
Spears are what's best for plundering.

250
00:17:18,721 --> 00:17:20,431
Really? Want to have a match?

251
00:17:25,021 --> 00:17:27,231
What's wrong with you?

252
00:17:27,311 --> 00:17:29,861
Don't throw everything on the floor.

253
00:17:29,941 --> 00:17:31,441
Hey. Are you listening to me?

254
00:17:31,941 --> 00:17:34,611
I'm going to throw it away
if you don't pick it up. Got it?

255
00:17:34,691 --> 00:17:36,701
Go ahead. I don't want it anymore.

256
00:17:39,071 --> 00:17:42,491
What are you doing,
searching through the storage room?

257
00:17:42,581 --> 00:17:44,161
Where are our weapons?

258
00:17:44,251 --> 00:17:45,791
What? Weapons?

259
00:17:46,331 --> 00:17:48,291
I need a weapon.

260
00:17:48,791 --> 00:17:49,791
If I had a weapon...

261
00:17:50,751 --> 00:17:51,961
Are you thinking...

262
00:17:52,301 --> 00:17:56,131
you're going to become a warrior
and sail on your father's ship?

263
00:17:56,761 --> 00:17:59,841
I'm telling you now,
don't waste your time trying.

264
00:17:59,931 --> 00:18:01,811
A little kid like you can't do it.

265
00:18:06,061 --> 00:18:07,231
Thorfinn.

266
00:18:52,731 --> 00:18:54,191
It's beautiful.

267
00:19:05,871 --> 00:19:08,251
What is it? What's wrong, Ylva?

268
00:19:11,501 --> 00:19:13,961
Do you want a sword, Thorfinn?

269
00:19:15,631 --> 00:19:17,591
A sword is a tool for killing people.

270
00:19:18,511 --> 00:19:21,891
Who were you planning to kill with this?

271
00:19:23,721 --> 00:19:25,811
The... The enemy.

272
00:19:27,021 --> 00:19:29,731
Who is your enemy?

273
00:19:32,191 --> 00:19:33,061
Like...

274
00:19:33,521 --> 00:19:35,231
Halfdan.

275
00:19:39,741 --> 00:19:41,651
Listen closely, Thorfinn.

276
00:19:48,701 --> 00:19:50,541
You don't have any enemies.

277
00:19:51,581 --> 00:19:54,461
No one has any enemies.

278
00:20:00,011 --> 00:20:03,431
There's no one who it's okay to hurt.

279
00:20:07,721 --> 00:20:10,221
You're wrong.

280
00:20:10,601 --> 00:20:13,731
Father, you're going off to war tomorrow.

281
00:20:14,231 --> 00:20:16,191
You're going to kill the enemy, right?

282
00:20:18,401 --> 00:20:19,731
I'm not a kid anymore.

283
00:20:20,281 --> 00:20:22,111
You're lying, Father.

284
00:20:22,401 --> 00:20:23,911
I can tell.

285
00:20:26,031 --> 00:20:27,161
Thorfinn.

286
00:20:27,781 --> 00:20:29,371
Thorfinn.

287
00:20:29,451 --> 00:20:32,121
-You let your guard down.
-That was dangerous.

288
00:20:32,211 --> 00:20:33,291
Hey.

289
00:20:33,371 --> 00:20:34,831
You made me bleed.

290
00:20:41,801 --> 00:20:42,841
Helga.

291
00:20:43,881 --> 00:20:44,971
Yes?

292
00:20:47,101 --> 00:20:49,761
Take care of him for me.

293
00:21:08,491 --> 00:21:10,661
The wind blows faintly from the west north-west.

294
00:21:10,741 --> 00:21:12,331
The waves are calm.

295
00:21:13,831 --> 00:21:16,171
Odin is in good spirits this morning.

296
00:21:17,211 --> 00:21:19,751
This is a good morning for your departure.

297
00:21:21,091 --> 00:21:21,921
Indeed.

298
00:21:27,721 --> 00:21:32,021
FAROE ISLANDS
STREYMOY

299
00:21:33,981 --> 00:21:35,521
You said it.

300
00:21:35,601 --> 00:21:39,111
If I throw left-handed and hit it,
the barrel is mine.

301
00:21:39,191 --> 00:21:41,021
-No way.
-You can talk after you hit it.

302
00:21:41,111 --> 00:21:42,111
I beg you, God...

303
00:21:42,611 --> 00:21:44,571
Here I go, Christian monk.

304
00:21:44,651 --> 00:21:46,611
If you dodge, I'll kill you.

305
00:21:50,491 --> 00:21:54,041
You bastard. You dodged.
You dodged just now. I'm going to kill you.

306
00:21:54,121 --> 00:21:55,501
Move. It's my turn.

307
00:21:59,131 --> 00:22:01,091
Oh, no. The priest...

308
00:22:02,251 --> 00:22:04,211
I told you not to dodge.

309
00:22:04,301 --> 00:22:06,511
You're just bad.

310
00:22:07,591 --> 00:22:10,301
Hey, Jomsvikings.

311
00:22:10,391 --> 00:22:12,261
Want to have a drink?

312
00:22:16,181 --> 00:22:18,101
They have good manners.

313
00:22:18,191 --> 00:22:19,311
Leave them alone.

314
00:22:19,401 --> 00:22:21,771
They said they don't like cheap alcohol.

315
00:22:22,191 --> 00:22:23,021
Hey.

316
00:22:25,231 --> 00:22:27,451
How many points do I get for his leg?

317
00:22:28,991 --> 00:22:33,531
Your men don't have any class, Askeladd.

318
00:22:34,991 --> 00:22:39,081
We just hate Christians, Floki.

319
00:22:40,121 --> 00:22:43,291
Enough about that. Let's get down to business.

320
00:22:44,671 --> 00:22:49,841
My men and I are bored of being kept here waiting
in the middle of nowhere.

321
00:22:50,891 --> 00:22:52,601
There are no major changes.

322
00:22:55,771 --> 00:22:57,931
You will be compensated with five pounds of gold.

323
00:22:58,311 --> 00:23:01,441
I will only pay you in exchange for his dead body.

324
00:23:02,481 --> 00:23:06,361
You can do whatever you want with their ship,
and their cargo.

325
00:23:09,281 --> 00:23:11,491
Kill Thors.
